    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d740-a1">

                <pb facs="0879" n="785" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg785"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 2621.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Dolz to Mr.
                            Williams.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Consulate-General</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-09-24"><hi rendition="#italic">September 24,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to Mr. Manuel Sanguily’s letter
                    of the 28th ultimo, addressed to the Hon. Alvey A. Adee, Acting Secretary of
                    State, and accompanying the Department’s instruction No. 1148 of the 9th
                    instant, I have to say that I never manifested to Mr. Julio Sanguily, imprisoned
                    at Fortress La Cabaña, in your name, “That as a result of an interview held by
                    you with General Arderius, acting Governor-General, that if he wished to be
                    released and sail to the United States he should demand it by means of a
                    petition.”</p>
                <p>Very respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. S. Dolz.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
